  "descriptions": {
    "preferred": "This outstanding dissectum from the Fratelli Gilardelli Nursery near Milan, Italy, is noted for the varying tones of green of the summer foliage with bronzed and redtinged new leaves at the shoot tips. The new leaves to about 1 mm at the leaf base. The green petioles are 3. 5-4 cm long. This cultivar forms a broad cascading mound up to 3-4 m tall with a spread of 4-5 m."
  },
